#: xml2xfconf:83
msgid ""
"xml2xfconf: convert xfce xfconf xml file entries into xfconf-query commands\n"
"\n"
"SUMMARY:    xml2xfconf -x|--xml-file <filepath> [-c|--channel "
"<channelname>]\n"
"\n"
"Passed an xfce xfconf xml file, this script will print\n"
"the necessary xfconf-query commands to update\n"
"the xfconf database for that channel.\n"
"\n"
"If passed a channel name, that will be compared with\n"
"the channel name defined in the xml,\n"
"and if they are different the script will exit.\n"
"\n"
"This is expected to be useful when restoring the xfconf settings of\n"
"an app whose xml file has been backed up.\n"
"\n"
"USAGE EXAMPLE:\n"
"\n"
"restore=$(mktemp);\n"
"xml2xfconf -x /path/to/xfce4-terminal.xml -c xfce4-terminal > \"$restore\";\n"
"bash \"$restore\"\n"
msgstr ""

